PLAY - a place to experiment

  sample.txt   about 2K of text to read, edit, copy and count
  wstat.c      a K&R C program that counts the words in a file
  vgfx.b09     a BASIC09 program that draws on the video screen
  readme       this file

Try the text:

  list sample.txt
  minted sample.txt
  tee <sample.txt >copy.txt

Build and run wstat (Level 2 mega images only: they carry the C
compiler, with its headers in /dd/DEFS and its library in /dd/LIB):

  chd /dd/play
  cc1 wstat.c
  wstat sample.txt

cc1 puts the finished program in your execution directory (/dd/cmds),
so wstat runs from anywhere, and leaves behind c.com, the command file
it ran; delete it when you like.

Ideas for changing wstat:

  - Treat an apostrophe as part of a word, so "don't" is one word.
  - Count the digits as well as the letters.
  - Print the ten most common words.
  - Draw the bars sideways, one column per letter.

Run vgfx (Level 2 mega images only: they carry BASIC09 and GFX2).
Run it on a video window, /V0 or /W1-/W7, not the serial console:

  chd /dd/play
  basic09
  load vgfx.b09
  run vgfx
  bye

It draws four scenes, waiting for Enter after each.  The drawing goes
through GFX2, the CoCo 3 graphics package for BASIC09 (in /dd/cmds on
the mega images): RUN GFX2("Line",x1,y1,x2,y2), "Circle", "Bar",
"Color", "Palette" and the rest send the CoCo 3 window codes, which the
video pico understands.  One difference from a CoCo 3: coordinates are
the panel's own pixels, 0-1023 across and 0-479 down, not scaled.
